course: dictionary
lesson: 11633
title: A word that shines: argent
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Argent is an old word for silver, or silvery in colour. You will mostly meet it in history lessons about knights, shields and coats of arms, and in old poems and stories. «The argent moon lit up the frozen lake.» The moon is bright and silvery, and lit up shows it is shining, so argent must mean silver.
explain: Argent can be a colour name or an adjective that describes something. In a history lesson you might read, «The shield was argent, with a red cross.» Here argent is the colour silver or white. When you are not sure, swap in silver and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Argent is one of the special colour names used in heraldry, the art of coats of arms. Gules means red, azure means blue, or means gold, and argent means silver or white. If you see the four names together, they are a code for colours.
fact: Argent means silver, or silvery in colour.
fact: In heraldry (the study of coats of arms), argent means silver or white.
fact: Argent is an old-fashioned, poetic word, so you will find it more in stories and poems than in everyday talk.
fact: In French, «argent» means both silver and money, and it is said as «ar-ZHAHN».
fact: The chemical symbol for silver, Ag, comes from the Latin word «argentum», and Argentina's name also comes from this word.
exercise: «The knight's shield was argent, with a red cross on it.» What does argent mean here? | Red | *Silver or white | Blue | Gold
exercise: In French, what does «argent» mean? | *Silver and money | Gold | Red | Water
exercise: «The argent moon lit up the frozen lake.» Find and copy one word that means silver or silvery. | frozen | moon | *argent | lake
test: In heraldry, which colour is argent? | Red | *Silver or white | Blue | Gold
test: Gules means red, azure means blue and or means gold. Which name means silver? | Or | *Argent | Gules | Azure
exam: The poem said, «Argent stars glimmered above the sea.» What does argent most likely mean? | Dark and cold | *Silvery and bright | Heavy and wet | Soft and warm
